{\pard\sb300\sa120{\f1\fs26\b\cf2 1. Company Overview}\par}
{\pard\sa200{\f1\fs20 Mejores Rese\u241?as is a market research and SaaS platform that helps small and medium-sized businesses in Mexico 舒? primarily restaurants, caf\'e9s, and service businesses in Ciudad Ju\'e1rez and Chihuahua 舒? improve their Google Business Profile visibility and earn more legitimate customer reviews.\par}}
{\pard\sa200{\f1\fs20 Our platform provides business owners with keyword demand data, review management guidance, and local SEO insights based entirely on ethical, Google-compliant practices. We do not facilitate, generate, or recommend fake or purchased reviews under any circumstances.\par}}

{\pard\sb300\sa120{\f1\fs26\b\cf2 2. Purpose of Google Ads API Access}\par}
{\pard\sa120{\f1\fs20 We are requesting access to the Google Ads API exclusively to retrieve {\b keyword search volume and competitive demand data} for internal market research. No advertising campaigns are created, managed, or modified.\par}}
{\pard\sa80{\f1\fs20\b Specifically, we use:}\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80{\f1\fs20\bullet\tab {\b KeywordPlanIdeaService.generateKeywordHistoricalMetrics} 舒? to retrieve average monthly searches, competition level, competition index, and top-of-page bid ranges for a predefined list of Spanish and English keywords related to Google reviews, Google Business Profile, and local SEO.}\par}
{\pard\li360\sa200{\f1\fs20\bullet\tab Geographic targeting: Mexico (geo ID 2484), Chihuahua state (geo ID 21177), Ciudad Ju\'e1rez (geo ID 1010166). Language targeting: Spanish (language ID 1003).}\par}
{\pard\sa80{\f1\fs20\b We do NOT use the API to:}\par}
{\pard\li360\sa60{\f1\fs20\bullet\tab Create, modify, or delete advertising campaigns, ad groups, or ads}\par}
{\pard\li360\sa60{\f1\fs20\bullet\tab Access or manage any third-party client ad accounts}\par}
{\pard\li360\sa60{\f1\fs20\bullet\tab Automate bidding, budgets, or targeting decisions}\par}
{\pard\li360\sa200{\f1\fs20\bullet\tab Perform any write or mutate operations of any kind}\par}

{\pard\sb300\sa120{\f1\fs26\b\cf2 3. Tool Architecture & Data Flow}\par}
{\pard\sa120{\f1\fs20\b Step 1 舒? Seed keyword list}\par}
{\pard\sa120{\f1\fs20 A curated, manually reviewed list of approximately 50 seed keywords in Spanish and English is maintained in a local DuckDB database. Keywords are categorized by intent (informational, commercial, navigational) and compliance risk. Risky or non-compliant intent keywords (e.g., 舠?buy fake reviews舡?) are stored for competitive awareness only and are never used as API inputs.}\par}
{\pard\sa120{\f1\fs20\b Step 2 舒? API call}\par}
{\pard\sa120{\f1\fs20 The Python script {\f2\fs18 scripts/02_google_ads_keywords.py} calls {\f2\fs18 KeywordPlanIdeaService.generateKeywordHistoricalMetrics} with the keyword list, geo targets, and language constant. The script is run manually by the developer; it is not scheduled or automated.}\par}
{\pard\sa120{\f1\fs20\b Step 3 舒? Raw storage}\par}
{\pard\sa120{\f1\fs20 API responses are written as immutable, date-stamped Apache Parquet files to a local directory ({\f2\fs18 data/raw/google_ads/YYYY-MM-DD/}). These files are never committed to version control.}\par}
{\pard\sa120{\f1\fs20\b Step 4 舒? Normalization & analysis}\par}
{\pard\sa200{\f1\fs20 A DuckDB analytics database reads the Parquet files, normalizes the data (accent/casing variants, deduplication), applies confidence scores (Google Ads values are marked {\f2\fs18 is_bucketed = true} since volumes are rounded), and stores results in structured tables for internal reporting.}\par}

